From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 09:05:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Convert system memory input on the CPU into the D3D
 output sample.

The video processor's D3D11 path (re-enabled for MSFS 2024) is taken
whenever its allocator gave a D3D output sample, even when the input
sample is in system memory, which video_processor_process_output_d3d11()
cannot use. It fails, and the fallback then allocates a CPU output
sample: a caller that gave the source reader a DXGI device manager gets
a memory sample. Unity's VideoPlayer queries IMFDXGIBuffer on it and
stops ("WindowsVideoMedia error 0x80004002, QueryInterface
IMFDXGIBuffer").

Take the D3D11 path only when both samples are D3D11 textures
(video_processor_can_use_d3d11(), as for caller-provided samples), and
otherwise convert on the CPU into the D3D output sample, as before the
D3D11 path was re-enabled.

Game impacted: Big Foot Crush (UNIS, Unity 2022): its MPEG-4 Part 2
decoder outputs system memory samples (0113), the video processor
converts them to ARGB32 for the VideoPlayer.
---
--- a/dlls/winedmo/video_processor.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/video_processor.c
@@ -1592,7 +1592,9 @@
         if (impl->device_manager
                 && SUCCEEDED(video_processor_init_allocator(impl))
                 && SUCCEEDED(IMFVideoSampleAllocatorEx_AllocateSample(impl->allocator, &output_sample)))
-            use_d3d11_processor = TRUE;
+            /* system memory input (a decoder without D3D samples) is converted on the CPU
+             * into the D3D output sample */
+            use_d3d11_processor = video_processor_can_use_d3d11(input_sample, output_sample);
         else if (FAILED(hr = video_processor_allocate_cpu_sample(impl, &output_sample)))
         {
             IMFSample_Release(input_sample);
-- 
2.51.0
